# Copy this file into your tracking folder as ".gitattributes" (note the
# leading dot, no .template extension).
#
# Why this file matters: Git normally "helps" by converting line endings in
# text files. Applied to binary files (images, sounds, archives) that
# conversion silently CORRUPTS them. The lines below tell Git which file
# types are binary and must never be touched.

# Treat everything else as text with Windows line endings.
* text eol=crlf

# Binary formats - must never go through line-ending conversion.
*.brarchive binary
*.nbt binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.tga binary
*.fsb binary
*.ogg binary
*.webm binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.fontdata binary
*.hdr binary
*.dat binary
*.mcstructure binary

# Extract-Brarchives.ps1 automatically maintains an extra block below this
# file's contents for individual binary .json files (compiled "MCB" files
# that could not be converted back to readable JSON). Do not edit that block
# by hand; the script rewrites it on every run.
